  "helpMessage": "Use each of the four numbers once and build an equality. The = sign is already on the board.\n\nOperators by difficulty:\n• Easy: + − × ÷, parentheses, √, ∛, !, **, |x|, ⌊x⌋ and ⌈x⌉. It is the only level that allows non-integer division (5/2).\n• Intermediate: the same, without floor and ceiling.\n• Advanced: + − × ÷, parentheses, √, ! and |x|.\n• Hard: + − × ÷, parentheses and |x|.\n\nFunctions take a group, √ (8 + 1), or a single number, √ 9. A minus sign before a group negates it: −(2 − 5) = 3.\n\nTap a piece on the board to remove it, and use Skip if a challenge is too hard.",
